                    {
                      "ref_index": 22,
                      "ref_type": "reddit",
                      "turn_index": 0
                    }
                  ],
                  "snippet": "Figure AI has unveiled a significant breakthrough in robotics, showcasing two of its F.03 humanoid robots autonomously cleaning a room and making a bed in under two minutes. The robots coordinate exclusively through visual signals like head nods—without explicit communication—demonstrating sophisticated AI capabilities. The demonstration, captured at normal speed, involved the robots hanging up a coat and headphones, closing a laptop, and collaboratively straightening a comforter, all while adapting to the dynamic nature of their environment.\n\nFigure AI highlighted three major challenges: the need for real-time coordination between the robots, managing the unpredictable shape of bedding, and adapting movement across varied tasks. The robots were trained using new data to handle complex actions like opening doors and moving furniture. Despite not announcing a consumer release date, the company, valued at $39 billion with over $1 billion raised, is a major competitor to Tesla's Optimus robot.\n\nFigure CEO Brett Adcock also parted ways with OpenAI to develop AI models independently, stating his goal to build a new species of self-learning, knowledge-sharing robots. This development aligns with broader industry trends, including rising demand for high-quality data from startups training robots to perform domestic chores.",
